# tools/co/constel_naming_witness.rish -- the Constel naming law, read both ways and both directions.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. A Constel name is a fake dev-network constellation stood up inside the jailed pier.
# Its one load-bearing promise is that it can never parse as a real @p, so a dev command a newcomer
# copies can never address a stranger's ship. The tree proves that promise TWICE, from two rounds a
# day apart, and the two proofs admit different sets of names:
#
#   digit present  -- seated 20260813. A real @p body is lowercase letters and hyphens only, drawn
#                     from a fixed 256-syllable table holding no digits. Mirrored in Rye by
#                     pond/apps/constel_net.rye's name_safe, which refuses UnsafeName without one.
#   vowel-free     -- seated 20260814, and the law constel/name.rye check_ship enforces. Every one
#                     of the 512 real syllables carries exactly one vowel and `y` is absent from the
#                     table, so a vowel-free name can never be assembled from them.
#
# Both are sound proofs of non-@p, so the SAFETY promise has never been in question. What the tree
# lacked was any reading of the two together: every one of the five names
# tools/fixtures/c/constel_names.txt seated carried a vowel, so constel/handshake.rye -- which calls
# check_ship and check_constellation at its border -- would have refused every name the ten
# pond/apps/constel_net*.rye modules use, and FORA31, the socket rung, is where they would first
# have met (REDS %306).
#
# THE REDRAW, 20260828. The five were redrawn as each elder name with its vowels dropped --
# xnqvel34 -> xnqvl34, xzkerith58 -> xzkrth58, xwmur-dol12 -> xwmr-dl12, maqwintel06 -> mqwntl06,
# sunveknar90 -> snvknr90 -- so the kinship to the elder draw stays readable in one glance and
# BOTH proofs now stand on every seated name. Dropping vowels rather than drawing fresh strings is
# what keeps the digit proof: constel/name.rye's alphabet is consonants AND decimal digits, so a
# name can satisfy the elder reading and the seated one at once. The seated draw's split now reads
# zero in both directions, and both numbers are pinned below.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal.
#   The welcome, as hard as the refusal: seven names constel/name.rye's own selftest asserts lawful
#   are admitted by the scan, case for case, so the shell reading and the Rye reading agree rather
#   than merely coexist.
#   The refusal: a galaxy, a star, two planet halves, and a whole planet -- the exact real @p shapes
#   the module refuses -- are refused, each by VowelPresent, with verdict=unsafe and a failing exit.
#   Every named fault the module can return from a names file: NameTooLong, BadCharacter, and
#   BadSegment, each planted and each answered with the module's own spelling.
#   The elder planted negative still bites at the same name it always named.
#
# WHAT IS STILL REPORTED RATHER THAN GATED, and it is the OTHER direction. split_digit_absent --
# names the seated vowel-free law admits and the elder digit proof turns away. It reads 6 of the 7
# names in the law fixture, and it is pinned below so that number cannot drift unread.
# constel/name.rye's own generate() lives entirely on that side: it draws the "xn" silo prefix plus
# base-21 digits over the CONSONANT palette and never emits a decimal digit, so every name it
# produces is refused UnsafeName by pond/apps/constel_net.rye's name_safe -- and constel/roster.rye
# already draws its roster that way. Which of the two rooms moves is a seat rather than this guard's
# call; the guard's job is to keep the number in front of a reader on every run.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That a Constel name is a good name, that pond/apps and constel/ should share
# one predicate rather than two, or which of the two rooms should move. This rung makes the split a
# number on every run; which way it closes is a seat.
#
# Law: active-designing/20260814-fill-constel-naming-law.md (seated)
#      active-designing/date/20260813/20260813-022222_constel-test-network-naming-law.md (elder)
# Output convention: context/specs/20260729-215600_scan-seam-convention.md.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/co/constel_naming_witness.rish

say "constel: Language EN -- fake dev constellations that can never reach the real network."
say "constel: Style Gauge, Meter -- two proofs of one promise, and the number where they part."
say "constel: Lens TAME -- safety first: the union gate never weakens, and the split is only reported."

# The welcome. Every name here is one constel/name.rye's selftest asserts lawful, so a green line
# means the shell mirror and the module agree case for case rather than by eye.
let law = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/constel_naming_scan.sh" "tools/fixtures/c/constel_names_law.txt"]
say law.out
assert law.ok else "constel: the law's own admitted names must pass free"
assert law.out contains "verdict=ok" else "constel: a name the module admits was refused by its shell mirror"
assert law.out contains "names=7" else "constel: the law fixture's own count changed unexpectedly"
assert law.out contains "seated_admitted=7" else "constel: every name in the law fixture must be admitted by the seated law"
assert law.out contains "never_a_ship=7" else "constel: every lawful name is provably never a real @p"
assert law.out contains "split_seated_refuses=0" else "constel: the seated law must never turn away its own examples"
# The open direction, pinned so it cannot drift unread: six of these seven lawful names carry no
# digit, so pond/apps/constel_net.rye's name_safe refuses them though check_ship admits them. This
# is where constel/name.rye's generate() output lives. Read the header before moving this number.
assert law.out contains "split_digit_absent=6" else "constel: the open direction's number moved -- six of the law fixture's seven names are vowel-free with no digit, which pond/apps name_safe refuses; read why before changing it"
assert (law.out contains "fault=") == false else "constel: a lawful name must carry no fault"

# The refusal, planted from the module's own selftest -- the exact shapes a newcomer might copy.
let real_ap = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/constel_naming_scan.sh" "tools/fixtures/c/constel_names_real_ap.txt"]
say real_ap.out
assert (real_ap.ok == false) else "constel: a real @p must refuse, and the status must say so"
assert real_ap.out contains "verdict=unsafe first=zod" else "constel: the scan must name the first real @p it met"
assert real_ap.out contains "fault=VowelPresent" else "constel: a real @p is refused by its vowel, by name"
assert real_ap.out contains "names=5" else "constel: the real @p fixture's own count changed unexpectedly"
assert real_ap.out contains "never_a_ship=0" else "constel: neither proof may admit a real @p"
assert real_ap.out contains "seated_admitted=0" else "constel: the seated law must admit no real @p"
assert real_ap.out contains "digit_bearing=0" else "constel: a real @p carries no digit, which is the elder proof's whole point"

# Each named fault the module can return from a names file, planted one per line.
let faults = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/constel_naming_scan.sh" "tools/fixtures/c/constel_names_faults.txt"]
say faults.out
assert (faults.ok == false) else "constel: a planted fault must refuse, and the status must say so"
assert faults.out contains "fault=NameTooLong" else "constel: a name past max_ship_len must refuse by name"
assert faults.out contains "fault=BadCharacter" else "constel: a byte outside the alphabet must refuse by name"
assert faults.out contains "fault=BadSegment" else "constel: a stray hyphen must refuse by name"
assert faults.out contains "names=5" else "constel: the fault fixture's own count changed unexpectedly"
assert faults.out contains "seated_admitted=0" else "constel: no planted fault may be admitted"

# The elder planted negative, kept whole: it bites at the same name it has always named.
let planted = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/constel_naming_scan.sh" "tools/fixtures/c/constel_names_unsafe.txt"]
say planted.out
assert planted.out contains "verdict=unsafe" else "constel: the scan failed to flag an @p-shaped name"
assert planted.out contains "first=sarlev" else "constel: the scan did not name the offending @p-shaped draw"
assert (planted.ok == false) else "constel: the unsafe verdict and status disagree"

# The seated draws, after the 20260828 redraw. Safe by the elder proof -- every one carries a digit
# -- AND admitted by the seated law, every one, because every one is vowel-free. Both readings agree
# on all five, which is what the redraw bought, so the whole split reads zero here.
let seated = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/constel_naming_scan.sh" "tools/fixtures/c/constel_names.txt"]
say seated.out
assert seated.ok else "constel: a seated constel name is safe under neither proof -- it could parse as a real @p"
assert seated.out contains "verdict=ok" else "constel: every seated name must be provably never a real @p"
assert seated.out contains "names=5" else "constel: the seated draw count changed unexpectedly"
assert seated.out contains "digit_bearing=5" else "constel: every seated draw carries the elder proof's digit"
assert seated.out contains "never_a_ship=5" else "constel: every seated draw is provably never a real @p"
assert seated.out contains "seated_admitted=5" else "constel: every seated draw must be admitted by the seated vowel-free law -- this is what the redraw closed"
assert seated.out contains "split_seated_refuses=0" else "constel: the seated law turned away a seated draw -- REDS %306 reopened; the redraw of 20260828 closed this and it may not regress"
assert seated.out contains "split=0" else "constel: a seated draw must carry BOTH proofs -- the two readings may not part on a name this tree seats"

say "GREEN: constel -- both proofs of the one promise read on every run: seven lawful names admitted case for case against constel/name.rye's own selftest, a galaxy and a planet refused VowelPresent, NameTooLong and BadCharacter and BadSegment each answered in the module's own spelling, the elder planted @p still biting at sarlev, and every seated draw provably never a real @p under BOTH readings -- split_seated_refuses=0 and split=0 on the seated draw, which is REDS %306 closed by the 20260828 redraw and pinned so it cannot regress, with split_digit_absent=6 keeping the one direction still open in front of a reader: the vowel-free names carrying no digit, where constel/name.rye generate() puts every name it draws"
